WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.635
GORDON RAMSAY: I've
still got lots to learn,

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.537
so I'm off to try a
traditional Christmas

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:08.475
dish that I hear tastes
much better than it smells.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:10.543
Now, trust me, I want to
get the best of Christopher,

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.948
and I'm up here to meet two guys
who make this amazing delicacy

00:00:15.014 --> 00:00:16.583
that can only be found here.

00:00:16.649 --> 00:00:19.319
[music playing]

00:00:19.386 --> 00:00:22.622
First of all, I'm
excited to see and taste

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:25.525
this incredible delicacy
that is rockfish.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:26.593
Rakfisk.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:27.227
[inaudible]

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.128
MAGNUS: Rakfisk.

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:29.596
- Fisk.
- Fisk.

00:00:29.662 --> 00:00:30.497
Rakfisk.

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.131
Rakfisk.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:32.065
Rakfisk.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.066
Rockfish, no.
Rakfisk.

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:33.900
Rakfisk.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.335
OK.

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.936
(VOICEOVER) After what
seems like hours are saying

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.939
the same thing back and forth,
[inaudible] and his nephew

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:43.410
Magnus show me how they make
the crown jewel of their family

00:00:43.476 --> 00:00:45.945
business-- fermented fish.

00:00:46.012 --> 00:00:46.813
What a smell.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:47.814
Very strong.

00:00:47.881 --> 00:00:48.848
Is that normal, that strong?

00:00:48.915 --> 00:00:49.983
MAGNUS: Yeah.

00:00:50.049 --> 00:00:50.917
Trout, and what
is that one there?

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:51.918
This is Arctic char.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:52.952
GORDON RAMSAY: Arctic char.

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:53.987
And how long do you cure it for?

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.255
It's in for three months.

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:56.623
GORDON RAMSAY: Bloody hell.

00:00:56.689 --> 00:01:00.226
So you pack it with
salt. And then--

00:01:00.293 --> 00:01:01.728
Sugar as well.
GORDON RAMSAY: Sugar.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:02.595
So it cures it.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:03.396
Yeah, exactly.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:04.831
And how old is this method?

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.399
Dates back to the Viking age.

00:01:06.466 --> 00:01:09.002
Now it's more popular than ever.

00:01:09.068 --> 00:01:10.503
Shall we?

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:13.573
MAGNUS: First, you put salt
in the belly, like this.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.508
And you just put
them in the bucket.

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.243
And then it's
heads, tails, heads,

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.446
tails all the way through.

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.313
Opposite.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.848
And you build.
MAGNUS: Exactly.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.583
GORDON RAMSAY: (VOICEOVER)
Sounds pretty straightforward--

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:24.651
or so I thought.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.920
But the rakfisk master
is not impressed.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:27.921
Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh.

00:01:27.987 --> 00:01:29.088
Too much?
MAN: Too much.

00:01:29.155 --> 00:01:29.923
Too much.

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.057
Less.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:31.958
Less salt. How's
that one, uncle?

00:01:32.025 --> 00:01:32.892
MAN: Ah, good.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:33.793
Good?

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.094
Thank god for that.

00:01:35.161 --> 00:01:36.629
I've never seen this
method before like this.

00:01:36.696 --> 00:01:39.699
It's only here in the
[inaudible] and [inaudible]..

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.901
GORDON RAMSAY: So it literally
is indigenous to this area.

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:42.836
MAGNUS: It is.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.204
We're very proud.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:47.307
It's very popular,
especially around Christmas.

00:01:47.373 --> 00:01:50.543
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.177
Little more.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.312
Little more.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.113
MAGNUS: You have
to use your wrist.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:56.816
Nei, nei, nei, nei.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:57.817
So.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:01:58.952
That's it?

00:01:59.018 --> 00:01:59.919
Perfect.

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:01.754
Man, your uncle's amazing.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:02.789
Do you ever upset him?

00:02:02.856 --> 00:02:04.190
Yeah, a lot of times.

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:05.225
It's better.
Good.

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.159
GORDON RAMSAY: Good?
Better.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:07.293
He's happy now.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.628
He's been a little
bit tough on me.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:10.296
Yeah, have been with
me for 10 years as well.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:11.965
GORDON RAMSAY: He's
a proper Viking.

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.132
I'm dying to taste it.
- Perfect.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:14.133
Oh, there it is there.

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:15.702
Wow, that's it there.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:22.876
Yeah.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.210
It's strong.

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:25.912
It's this cross between
a sort of cured salmon

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.748
but with a Vacheron cheese.

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.917
It was so strong, very acidic.

00:02:30.984 --> 00:02:32.085
This is not very strong.

00:02:32.151 --> 00:02:33.353
That's not very strong?

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:34.120
No.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.121
Let's try a stronger one.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.256
No, stop it.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.123
MAGNUS: Let's try it.
- Really?

00:02:37.190 --> 00:02:38.324
Stronger than that?

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:40.660
Let's try our special
Christmas batch.

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:41.895
Bloody hell.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:44.597
(VOICEOVER) I'm worried
that special, in this case,

00:02:44.664 --> 00:02:45.999
is not a good thing.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.967
So what's special
about this batch?

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.335
MAGNUS: We have had
it in the barrel

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:51.070
for a longer amount of time.

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.673
Now, oh, my god,
the smell of that.

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.842
Bloody hell.

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.176
Pfft.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.279
It doesn't look very appetizing.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.048
And the smell gets stronger
the farther down the bucket

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:02.882
you go.

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:04.150
Bloody hell.

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:05.451
Seriously.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:07.053
Oh my god.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.254
This is sticky as--

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.189
[chuckles] Don't [bleep] around.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:12.091
You don't eat this, do you?

00:03:12.158 --> 00:03:12.926
Oh my god.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.826
Mm.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:14.661
You like that smell?

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:15.528
Yeah.

00:03:15.595 --> 00:03:16.596
Oh, no.

00:03:16.663 --> 00:03:19.566
[bleep] No.

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:20.867
Look at the juice.

00:03:20.934 --> 00:03:22.001
The color of the juice.

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.202
MAGNUS: That's
the right texture.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:26.105
Can you cut that, please?

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:27.774
Is this a joke?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.108
Oh my lord.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:30.176
Oh my god.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.077
It's like putty.

00:03:31.144 --> 00:03:33.212
Why is this so--

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:35.582
a special rare delicacy
when it stinks?

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.550
You should not
think about the smell.

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:40.620
It's the flavor.

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:41.454
Don't!

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.256
[chuckling]

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.059
GORDON RAMSAY: No, no, no.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:47.694
MAGNUS: That's
the right texture.

